From 9175a7a460b9729486cbf345f9dd5b7073f1760d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dini Senanayake <dini.senanayake@kennedy.ox.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:54:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply Slurm account and partition to every job via
 --default-resources

- Move account/partition to a top-level 'slurm:' config section; they are
  cluster-level settings, not per-rule resources.
- CLI passes them as --default-resources so rules with bespoke resources
  (hisat_index build, salmon quant, bamqc CollectRnaSeqMetrics) are covered.
- CLI validated 'resources.account' while templates had moved to
  'resources.slurm_account'; now validates 'slurm.account', with legacy keys
  accepted and a deprecation warning.
- Fix sacctmgr lookups: '$USER' was passed literally (no shell), so account
  validation silently never ran.
- 'txseq <wf> config' pre-fills the user's default Slurm account.
- Hold 'threads' separately from the resources dict; fix hisat.smk
  referencing the removed 'hisat_thread' key.
